{"id":"GVPT459M","title":"Seminar in Comparative Politics; Social Movements","department":"Government and Politics","level":null,"credits":"3","description":"Prerequisite: GVPT200 or GVPT280. Restriction: Must be in Government & Politics program.\n\nDiscussion-intensive advanced seminar exploring the ways that social movements mobilize, the role of governments and bystanders in shaping that process, and the outcomes that they produce through connecting history, theory, and scholarship to contemporay politics. Special topics include youth movements and campus activism, transnationalism, and violent vs. non-violent strategies.","gradingMethods":"Reg, P-F, Aud","noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201801","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Kanisha Bond"],"removed":false},{"term":"201808","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Kanisha Bond"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":6,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Kanisha Bond"],"removed":false},{"term":"202001","sections":2,"seats":60,"openSeats":3,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Kanisha Bond"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":7,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Jennifer Hadden"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":1,"instructors":["Jennifer Hadden"],"removed":false},{"term":"202301","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Jennifer Hadden"],"removed":false},{"term":"202308","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Jennifer Hadden"],"removed":false}],"instructors":[{"name":"Jennifer Hadden","terms":4,"slug":"gvpt-jennifer-hadden"},{"name":"Kanisha Bond","terms":4,"slug":"gvpt-kanisha-bond"}]}